# Playwright e2e

## Commands

- `npm run test:e2e:install` — install Chromium browsers
- `npm run test:e2e` — full e2e suite (API health + desktop download + login page)
- `npm run test:e2e:api` — public API smoke only
- `npm run test:e2e:desktop` — desktop download smoke only

## Base URL

Override with `PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL`. Prefer:

1. Local during development: `http://localhost:3000`
2. Current Vercel production when verifying deploy: `https://asbatechs-crm-web.vercel.app`

Avoid assuming custom DNS hosts are on the latest commit unless Domains mapping is verified. Stale hosts often 404 `/api/desktop/installer` and serve older attendance policy JSON.

## Spec rules

- Prefer `getByRole` / `getByTestId` over fragile CSS.
- Desktop download CTA: `data-testid="desktop-download-btn"`.
- Do not assert on secrets or env-only content.
- API specs: assert status + `Content-Type: application/json` where expected; never accept 5xx for happy-path public APIs.
- Skip gracefully if installer API is 404 **only** on known-stale hosts; core download page on production should not show “Installer URL is not configured”.

## Delivery order (with agent-delivery)

After web/API changes: **Playwright → build → commit → push**. See `.cursor/rules/agent-delivery.mdc`.
